NOTES AND QUESTIONS ON RULE 48
What portions of Rule 48 set requirements on the jury that the parties can alter? Which portions can the parties not alter? Why do you think some requirements are treated differently in terms of how much control the parties, through agreement, can exercise over the size and decisionmaking process of the jury?

INTRODUCTORY NOTE TO HANS, GASTIL, AND FELLER, DELIBERATIVE DEMOCRACY AND BURGER, THINKING THE UNTHINKABLE
The doctrine, from Beacon Theatres to Colgrove, has struggled to make sense of text and history of the Seventh Amendment. Implicit, and sometimes explicit, in the Court’s dissertations on the Seventh Amendment have been policy concerns about what the civil jury is, or should be, accomplishing. If we set aside the doctrine and the constitutional text entirely, we might ask: What values do civil juries serve? What values should civil juries serve? What values do they disserve? What does this tell us about the desirability of civil juries as a policy matter? What does this tell us about the desirability of a right to civil juries as a policy matter?
